adr: 0220
file: selfhost/compiler.pas
kills: const_nullstring
why: A name bound to `''` possesses the canonical string-type, whose representation is a length word in front of the characters -- and the global holds the characters alone. Without this arm the value is read as though those four bytes were there, so what a program prints is whatever the linker put next in read-only data, for however many bytes the first four of them spell. It is invisible at -O2, where the out-of-bounds load folds to zero, which is why the case it kills carries a .opt sidecar saying -O0.
--- old
  else if StringConstOf(e) <> nil then begin
    lit := StringConstOf(e);
    EmitAddress(e, data);
    OpInt(lit^.stLen, len)
  end
--- new
  else if false then begin
    OpInt(0, len)
  end
